        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/4/n/camden-fort-meagher-wp/embarrassingly-basic-l.png",
          "filename": "LowerCorkHarbourBasicMap.png",
          "caption": "Embarrassingly basic layout \"map\" of Lower Cork Harbour in County Cork, Ireland. Expanded and largely hand-drawn from open/PD sources. Red highlighted areas indicate naval/military installations. (Some extant, some historic or demilitarised):\nA - Haulbowline Naval Base, HQ of the Irish Naval Service\nB - Fort Mitchel (previously Fort Westmoreland) on Spike Island\nC - Fort Meagher (previously Fort Camden) close to Crosshaven\nD - Fort Davis (previously Fort Carlisle) close to Whitegate\nE - Fort Templebreedy (or Templebreedy Battery)",
